cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mc34b-mod: a simulated 6P3S-E push-pull ultralinear tube amplifier, with stability, supply and tolerance studies"
authors:
  - family-names: Kao
    given-names: En-Tsai
    alias: heinricitorgau
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/heinricitorgau/mc34b-mod"
abstract: >-
  A simulation-only design study of a fixed-bias 6P3S-E push-pull ultralinear
  stereo tube amplifier (6N2 voltage amplifier, direct-coupled 6N1 long-tail
  pair) in LTspice and ngspice, taking the transformer specifications of the
  Ming-Da MC34-B as assumptions and an ELAC ELT 10 as the load. Includes tube
  models fitted to digitized datasheet curves, loop-stability analysis over a
  grid of output-transformer assumptions, power-supply and mains-variation
  simulation, Monte Carlo tube spread, and output-transformer saturation.
  Every figure is regenerated from the netlists by script.
keywords:
  - vacuum tube amplifier
  - SPICE
  - ngspice
  - LTspice
  - circuit simulation
  - loop stability
  - Monte Carlo
  - audio
